Branching map:
1. Cis regulatory haplotype -> mature gene RNA (promoter/enhancer, RNA processing/stability, or cell composition). eQTL tests association, not which route.
2. Cis haplotype -> intron excision / transcript structure. sQTL does not automatically mean promoter usage or RNA-end switch; join exact strand/assembly/transcript features only.
3. Apparent absence -> low coverage / selection / low power / genuine weak effect. All-tested tables distinguish these partially; significant-only absence cannot.
4. Cross-context concordance -> broadly shared regulation versus correlated donors/LD/composition. Independent cohort same variant/allele/feature test is discriminating; different tissues alone are transfer.
5. Lead region -> established cis feature versus unrelated LD-tagged neighbor. Exact human coordinates and perturbation evidence needed; no rat-coordinate transplant or visual colocalization.

Allocate substantive effort to independent evidence and annotation/coverage checks rather than repeated sensitivity on selected hits. Strongest useful endpoint is a reproducible association with a falsifiable regulatory hypothesis; absolute protein dose curve is outside these data.

